{
  "id": "candidate-applied-airfuel-cross-limit",
  "name": "Air\u2013Fuel Cross-Limiting Selector Control",
  "category": "engineering",
  "description": "Exact author air/oil transfer blocks expanded into output and output-rate states. Author101 sampled command values and linear interpolation are retained, including sample-grid ramps around nominal1s/15s steps. Cross-limit selectors preserve air lead during load changes. Primary model: \u00c5str\u00f6m and Murray, Feedback Systems, second edition, author BSD 3-Clause Python source pinned dbbc2e1b4233dc148a3dc52c10d08e87881c1f15. Numerical grid is our explicit choice. No empirical calibration or safety-control guarantee. Units not supplied where a coherent physical annotation has not been established.",
  "source": "https://github.com/murrayrm/fbs2e-python/blob/dbbc2e1b4233dc148a3dc52c10d08e87881c1f15/figure-1.18-airfuel_selectors.py",
  "reference": "\u00c5str\u00f6m and Murray, Feedback Systems, second edition; author example code figure-1.18-airfuel_selectors.py",
